WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:03.259
Continuing from where we left off,

2
00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:06.259
is the importing and exporting within Unreal Engine.

3
00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:08.539
So we're going to hop right into the engine here

4
00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:10.839
and take a look at the project first,

5
00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:13.679
and then we are going to play around with importing

6
00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.600
and exporting so we can get used to some of these menus.

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.940
So let's hop in to the engine.

8
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.940
So after you've opened up your project,

9
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.219
you should see something very similar to this,

10
00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:25.899
in which we have a folder over here

11
00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:28.140
on the left for the animation class.

12
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.719
Now, you will notice it is blank,

13
00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:32.020
but this is where we can work to keep

14
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:32.920
things organized.

15
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.020
This is where you can import your animations,

16
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.490
as well as any characters that you're going to bring in.

17
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.710
Then over here, if you open this little carrot up,

18
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.869
you will see meshes and a lot of different characters

19
00:00:43.869 --> 00:00:45.189
involved with this.

20
00:00:45.189 --> 00:00:46.630
The one we are going to work with today

21
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.130
is the Stackebot.

22
00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.909
So go ahead and click on that.

23
00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:51.450
Then you're going to open your characters folder

24
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.049
and into the bot folder.

25
00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:55.890
You'll notice there's quite a few folders as well,

26
00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.570
but the ones we want to concern ourselves with today

27
00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.210
is the mesh and the animations folder.

28
00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.329
Now for importing, we're going to kind of cheat a little bit

29
00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:07.969
and use an existing mesh and then bring it back.

30
00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:09.069
But we're going to utilize that

31
00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.909
through the animations folder.

32
00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:13.290
So let's begin with that.

33
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.450
Now that we're in our folder,

34
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.810
let's go ahead and head towards the animations folder.

35
00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.010
Inside, you're going to find

36
00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:22.769
multiple animation sequences for Stackebot,

37
00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:27.010
but I'm going to choose the Abot Walk animation sequence.

38
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.090
I'm not going to open it yet.

39
00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.969
All I'm going to do is I'm going to right click on this

40
00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:33.989
and we're going to want to look for asset actions and export.

41
00:01:33.989 --> 00:01:36.590
So let's go ahead and export.

42
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.590
You're going to get a place to,

43
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.109
where do you want to save this?

44
00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:40.670
I'm just going to do it in my downloads

45
00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.290
as it'll be a little easier to find.

46
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.230
And then another window is going to pop up.

47
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.109
This is the FBX export options.

48
00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:51.989
Now going over these just briefly,

49
00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:53.950
the only thing you really need to check on

50
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.409
will be down here for the preview mesh.

51
00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:59.109
You want to make sure that that is checked on.

52
00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:01.109
Now mine is saved on by default,

53
00:02:01.109 --> 00:02:03.349
but if you ever notice this is not checked,

54
00:02:03.349 --> 00:02:08.030
it's because you have not reset to default and it's blank.

55
00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.150
So what you want to make sure this is checked on.

56
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.460
All the others you can leave on by default,

57
00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.699
including the FBX 2013, and there are other versions,

58
00:02:16.699 --> 00:02:20.319
but FBX 2013 seems to work pretty well.

59
00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:21.879
Then you're going to click export

60
00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:24.039
and then you're going to look for it in your downloads.

61
00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:25.400
That was pretty much it.

62
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.680
There it is downloaded right there.

63
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.000
So that's what we want to do.

64
00:02:29.039 --> 00:02:32.039
So now we want to import that.

65
00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:33.360
Now there are multiple ways

66
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.439
that you can import into your folder.

67
00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:36.680
Now I said that we were going to use

68
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.759
this animation class folder to work out of.

69
00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.639
So what you want to do is find wherever it was

70
00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:43.439
that you saved and you can do two things.

71
00:02:43.439 --> 00:02:46.520
You can add it by importing,

72
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.819
or you can simply just drag and drop

73
00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:52.080
from wherever you saved it right into the folder.

74
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.520
I kind of prefer this a little bit more

75
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.680
and just because it's a little more efficient for me.

76
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.620
However, as soon as you do that,

77
00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.020
you are going to see the FBX import options.

78
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.560
Now this definitely has a lot more settings

79
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.759
than what the previous for exporting.

80
00:03:04.759 --> 00:03:06.460
So let's kind of go over these.

81
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:09.500
So it does show that it is a skeletal mesh.

82
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.819
The animation has it included.

83
00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.580
So what we want to tell to do is yes,

84
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.300
we do want to bring in the skeletal mesh

85
00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.500
because it's movable.

86
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.580
We also want to make sure to import the mesh

87
00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.099
that comes along with that.

88
00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.539
Now the import default is set to geometry

89
00:03:22.539 --> 00:03:23.539
and skinning weights.

90
00:03:23.539 --> 00:03:25.139
We're not going to go too deeply into that,

91
00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:26.340
but there are some other settings

92
00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.419
for various types of optimization.

93
00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:31.379
However, this one works really well for our purposes.

94
00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:32.800
Now, if we didn't have a skeleton,

95
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.639
we could assign it in a skeleton

96
00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:36.099
as you see all these multiple ones,

97
00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:37.580
but we're going to leave that as default.

98
00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.419
All right.

99
00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:40.379
And just bring as what is.

100
00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:41.699
Now, going down through here

101
00:03:41.699 --> 00:03:44.419
where there's a lot more settings, as you can see,

102
00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:46.180
and I can kind of expand upon that.

103
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.090
Going down through here.

104
00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.610
Now the use TO as reference pose,

105
00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.370
that's where you want to kind of make sure

106
00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.210
that it is in a T pose,

107
00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.409
and you're going to use that for the reference.

108
00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:57.770
So if it's in a different type of pose,

109
00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.009
you would want to check this on.

110
00:03:59.009 --> 00:04:01.169
It'll correct that for you,

111
00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:03.150
but we can leave that off by default.

112
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.490
Everything else, in fact,

113
00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.189
can be left on and off as defaults.

114
00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:09.189
The only thing you want to make sure

115
00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:11.629
you kind of go down through here is the animation.

116
00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:13.210
So if there is an animation,

117
00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.389
you'd want to go ahead and import those too.

118
00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:17.889
We're not going to do that in this case.

119
00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:19.649
Instead, we're just going to kind of go through here

120
00:04:19.649 --> 00:04:20.490
and go over it,

121
00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.629
but you could import your animations

122
00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.689
along with just importing the skeletal mesh.

123
00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.529
So let's just say we are going to do that.

124
00:04:26.529 --> 00:04:28.129
Click on import animation.

125
00:04:28.129 --> 00:04:30.610
You're going to notice these are all opened up for you.

126
00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.370
Now you can change all sorts of additional settings,

127
00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.889
like the frame import range.

128
00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:37.329
So say you want to only import like 10 seconds

129
00:04:37.329 --> 00:04:38.490
of whatever it was,

130
00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.329
you could adjust these here.

131
00:04:40.329 --> 00:04:42.730
But again, we're going to leave these as all default,

132
00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.649
except for the import animation,

133
00:04:44.649 --> 00:04:46.250
because we do want to bring along that animation

134
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:50.069
just to show you how the import export series works.

135
00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:52.490
There's quite a few of other settings that, again,

136
00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.589
we won't go over because these are more advanced topics.

137
00:04:55.589 --> 00:04:57.769
However, you could even convert the scene.

138
00:04:57.769 --> 00:04:59.970
You could force a front X axis,

139
00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.389
because typically it's not the same axis

140
00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:04.970
in other DCC programs.

141
00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.410
You could adjust that here.

142
00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.009
You could even convert the scene unit.

143
00:05:08.009 --> 00:05:09.290
So let's say, for example,

144
00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.250
you were working in meters and not centimeters,

145
00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.810
because obviously the default in Unreal

146
00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.550
is a one centimeter per unit.

147
00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.490
So you might find that the scene unit,

148
00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.569
you bring it in and everything's too large or too small.

149
00:05:21.569 --> 00:05:22.769
It could be because of that.

150
00:05:22.769 --> 00:05:23.889
So you can always come back

151
00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.730
and re-import it with this setting.

152
00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:26.569
However, like I said,

153
00:05:26.569 --> 00:05:28.769
we're going to leave everything else as default,

154
00:05:28.769 --> 00:05:30.850
including allowing it to create new materials

155
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.910
and just hit import all.

156
00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.990
And it doesn't take it too horribly long.

157
00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.069
And you're going to see everything

158
00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.509
that is attached with it.

159
00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:39.709
It'll bring in some materials.

160
00:05:39.709 --> 00:05:40.910
So you'll notice he's kind of broken.

161
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.949
It doesn't have the materials that he had before.

162
00:05:42.949 --> 00:05:44.069
So you will have to go through back

163
00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:46.310
and reassign those in this case.

164
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.709
But you'll see here, you've got your skeletal mesh,

165
00:05:48.709 --> 00:05:52.029
the animation sequence, as well as a physics asset,

166
00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.310
which we'll go over in a little bit

167
00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.029
and the skeleton along with the two materials,

168
00:05:56.029 --> 00:05:58.230
one material and one in instance.

169
00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.269
So this is what we want to do for simple importing

170
00:06:01.269 --> 00:06:03.029
from your asset as an FBX.

171
00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.870
This is what you're going to tend to see

172
00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.149
in your typical import.

173
00:06:07.149 --> 00:06:11.029
Another source of animations is on the Epic Games launcher

174
00:06:11.029 --> 00:06:12.470
through the marketplace.

175
00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.829
Here you can find a series of animations,

176
00:06:14.829 --> 00:06:16.829
both purchase and free,

177
00:06:16.829 --> 00:06:19.490
that you would be able to add to your project.

178
00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.910
Simply download it.

179
00:06:20.949 --> 00:06:22.029
And once it is downloaded,

180
00:06:22.029 --> 00:06:24.990
you'll notice this add to project option.

181
00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.389
All you have to do is click that

182
00:06:26.389 --> 00:06:28.269
and add it to the project that you wish to add.

183
00:06:28.269 --> 00:06:31.990
And voila, you have your animation to use.
